  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://purl.org/space-ontology/Satelite_Name">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purl.org/space-ontology/Identifier"/>
    <dc:creator rdf:resource="http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3835-7817"/>
    <dc:description xml:lang="en">The name of a satellite, expressed as an string of alphanumeric characters. The proper name for a satellite.</dc:description>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">satellite name</rdfs:label>
    <ns1:Example xml:lang="en">"International Space Station"</ns1:Example>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://purl.org/space-ontology/Sensor_Observation">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purl.org/space-ontology/Observation"/>
    <dc:creator rdf:resource="http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3835-7817"/>
    <dc:creator xml:lang="en">Robert John Rovetto</dc:creator>
    <dc:description xml:lang="en">A sensor observation (dataset) consists of the position and often the velocity of an object in outerspace taken at a particular time and relative to the obseving sensor.
As a data set of recorded quantities, a particular observation is an instance.</dc:description>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">"Observation" in the space situational awareness, astronautics, and astonomy communities is sometimes used ambiguously. It often refers to data collected by a sensor. 
An observation in the SSA community, for example, is typically understood as sensor data, or a dataset provided by sensors observing outerspace. A particular observation is a detection of an object in orbit.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">sensor observation</rdfs:label>
    <ns1:Alternative_Label xml:lang="en">observation</ns1:Alternative_Label>
    <ns1:Development_Status_Note xml:lang="en">Further development is needed to model what various astroautical groups call 'observations'. Differentiate between data, datasets, the activity of observation, the result of the observation (e.g. a dataset), etc.

Consider modeling observations as such... 
Distinguish between at least the act of observing, the observer, and the product of the activity. The observation of the orbital environments yields a dataset about detected objects in that environment. 

More precisely, the activity of observing is enacted by a space-based or ground-based sensor (an actor). That activity yields a observation dataset, i.e., a dataset recorded by the sensor. An observation often involves measuring some phenomena. Measurements an the activity of measuring should be represented, including the quantitative elements, such as units of distance and mass (e.g., meters and grams).

The genesis of the observation itself begins with electromagnetic energy being received by a sensor, recorded as data, processed, etc. That data may then be transitted from the sensor facility to another location (and actor).

Consider also an observation as a single event, as a single detection of an object in terms of azimuth and elevation relative to the sensor making the observation (see U.S. gov publication SD505).</ns1:Development_Status_Note>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://purl.org/space-ontology/has_Orbital_Property">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <dc:creator rdf:resource="http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3835-7817"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has orbital property</rdfs:label>
    <ns1:Alternative_Label xml:lang="en">has orbit property</ns1:Alternative_Label>
    <ns1:Development_Status_Note xml:lang="en">Under development.

Considering alternative labels to better allow for sub-relations that more precisely describe more specific relationships between types of orbit.</ns1:Development_Status_Note>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://purl.org/space-ontology/Owner">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purl.org/space-ontology/SSA_Actor"/>
    <dc:creator rdf:resource="http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3835-7817"/>
    <dc:description xml:lang="en">An actor or agent who legally owns the device or technological system in question.</dc:description>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">owner</rdfs:label>
    <ns1:Development_Status_Note xml:lang="en">This is not specific to the target domain. Consider subclasses such as 'Spacecraft Owner' and  'Launch Vehicle Owner' to more precisely characterize the intended meaning. A broader Owner category can be discpline-neutral, applying to spacelight as well as other disciplines.</ns1:Development_Status_Note>
  </rdf:Description>
