  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://purl.org/space-ontology/Space_Vehicle">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purl.org/space-ontology/Spacecraft"/>
    <dc:creator rdf:resource="http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3835-7817"/>
    <dc:creator xml:lang="en">Robert John Rovetto</dc:creator>
    <dc:description xml:lang="en">A spacecraft designed for self-propelled flight in outer space environment. 
A spacecraft designed for self-propelled flight in the microgravity environment.</dc:description>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Space Vehicles can specialize spacecraft as a type of spacecraft that is designed travel through space. 

Some spacecraft (or space artifacts) may be designed to remain in a relatively fixed spatial position, but not designed for motion or not designed for the stresses of self-propelled motion. However, given the nature of spaceraft engineering and spaceflight, it may not be correct; rather, all spacecrcaft may be designed for space travel.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Space Vehicle</rdfs:label>
    <ns1:Alternative_Label xml:lang="en">Astronautical Vehicle</ns1:Alternative_Label>
  </rdf:Description>
