  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://purl.org/space-ontology/Argument_of_Perigee">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purl.org/space-ontology/Argument_of_Periapsis"/>
    <dc:creator rdf:resource="http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3835-7817"/>
    <dc:description xml:lang="en">Argument of Perigee desribes the orientation of an orbit in its orbital plane relative to Earth. 
It defines where the low point, perigee, of the orbit is with respect to the Earth's surface (https://spaceflight.nasa.gov/realdata/elements/).
It is the angle, measured in the direction of satellite motion, from the Ascending Node to Perigee.
It has values greater than 0 but less than 360 degrees.
The angle from line of nodes to satellite position vector.
It's value is undefined when orbital inclination is 0 or 180 degrees, or when orbtal eccentricity is 0.
It is represented by Greek lowercase omega.</dc:description>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">argument of perigee</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
