  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://purl.org/space-ontology/Space_Situational_Awareness">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <dc:creator xml:lang="en">Robert J. Rovetto</dc:creator>
    <dc:description xml:lang="en">There are various definitions of  'space sitautiona awareness' (SSA).

SSA (relative to Earth) can be understood as awareness, or knowledge, of the orbital and near-Earth space environments. This involves understanding and predicting the motion of objects in that environment, how they are related to the environment, how they interact and behave, and what their characterisitcs are. This means that it is essential to understand the causal relationships among near-Earth objects, space weather, spacecraft and orbital debris. 
It can be conceived as the understanding derived from studying the near-Earth space environment (T.S. Kelso).

The SSA domain includes natural celestial bodies (e.g., near-Earth objects), space wheather phenomena, spacecraft, orbital debris, and the processed by which we observe and gain knowledge of those entities. 

An essential task of SSA is observing, detecting, tracking identifying and predicting the motion of objects in orbital space. Space surveillance is therefore important. This calls for understanding the wider orbital space environment, including the gravitational effects from various celestial bodies.

"Knowing the state of motion of objects in orbit, and estimating where those objects will be in the future, are central elements of space situational awareness." (Quote from "Space situational awareness and space traffic management standardization" by David Finkleman")

Achieving and maintaining SSA requires orbit determination (identifying where an object is now), orbit propagation/prediction (identifying where an object may be in the future), and assessing risk of collisions.</dc:description>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Space Situational Awareness</rdfs:label>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">space domain awarenss</skos:altLabel>
    <ns1:Alternative_Label xml:lang="en">SSA</ns1:Alternative_Label>
    <ns1:Alternative_Label xml:lang="en">Spaec Domain Awareness</ns1:Alternative_Label>
  </rdf:Description>
