    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has launch site</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://purl.org/space-ontology/Right_Ascension_of_the_Ascending_Node">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purl.org/space-ontology/Classical_Keplerian_Orbital_Element"/>
    <dc:description xml:lang="en">RAAN describes the rotation of the orbital plane about a central body such as Earth. It is the angle, measured eastward, from the vernal equanox to the ascending node.
It defines the location of the ascending and descending orbit locations with respect to the Earth's equatorial plane (https://spaceflight.nasa.gov/realdata/elements/).
It has values greater or equal to 0 but less than 360 degrees.
It's value is undefined for equatorial orbits, i.e., when inclination is 0 or 180 degrees.
It is a measure of the angle from the x-axis of the reference coordinate system to the line of nodes. E.g.,: the angle from vernal equinox direction to the line of nodes.</dc:description>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">right ascension of the ascending node</rdfs:label>
    <ns1:Alternative_Label xml:lang="en">RAAN</ns1:Alternative_Label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://purl.org/space-ontology/Identifier">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <dc:creator rdf:resource="http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3835-7817"/>
    <dc:creator xml:lang="en">Robert John Rovetto</dc:creator>
    <dc:description xml:lang="en">A string of characters (e.g., numeric, alphanumeric, etc.) that identifies, signifies, designates, or refers to something (e.g., spacecraft). Identifiers may be names, or sequences of numbers, etc.</dc:description>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">identifier</rdfs:label>
    <ns1:Alternative_Label xml:lang="en">Designator</ns1:Alternative_Label>
    <ns1:Alternative_Label xml:lang="en">ID</ns1:Alternative_Label>
    <ns1:Description_of_Class xml:lang="en">This class is intended to capture the various kinds of alphanumeric identifiers.
It can serve as a high-level backbone construct to facilitate interoperability among agents with their own identifiers for the same object.</ns1:Description_of_Class>
    <ns1:Development_Status_Note xml:lang="en">Edit and Organize hierarchy. Some subclasses may be deleted, but their respective labels/names may be declared as synonyms or alternative labels for others.

Consider the subclass of Alphanumeric Identifier.
Consider the subclass of Spacecraft Identifier, or Space Object Identifier.</ns1:Development_Status_Note>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://purl.org/space-ontology/Measurement">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <dc:creator rdf:resource="http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3835-7817"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">measurement</rdfs:label>
    <ns1:Development_Status_Note xml:lang="en">Disambiguate activity of measuring from the measurement (as in the numeric value, that may be the result of the activity).

Measurements are essential to SSA. Observations involve taking measurements, and therefore yield measurement data. The relationship between these and other related entities should be represented in the ontology.

A particular measurement indicates a value of the property of some property-bearing subject or object. For example, a measurement of the mass of an object is a specific value (e.g., 500 grams) for the mass property of the object.</ns1:Development_Status_Note>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://purl.org/space-ontology/has_Purpose">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <dc:creator rdf:resource="http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3835-7817"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has purpose</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://purl.org/space-ontology/Space_Shuttle">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purl.org/space-ontology/Spacecraft"/>
    <dc:creator rdf:resource="http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3835-7817"/>
    <dc:description xml:lang="en">A reusable spacecraft designed to carry persons and cargo..</dc:description>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Space Shuttle</rdfs:label>
    <ns1:Development_Status_Note xml:lang="en">Disambiguate 'space shuttle' as in the NASA Space Trasportation System (STS) vs. a generic term for any astronautical shuttle.</ns1:Development_Status_Note>
  </rdf:Description>
