  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/rrovetto/ontologies/2014/space-situational-awareness-ontology#has_name">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
    <dc:creator rdf:resource="http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3835-7817"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A relation linking a named object and the specific alphanumeric value of its Name, in a string.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has_name</rdfs:label>
    <ns1:Alternative_Label xml:lang="en">has name</ns1:Alternative_Label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://purl.org/space-ontology/Central_Body">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <dc:creator rdf:resource="http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3835-7817"/>
    <dc:description xml:lang="en">The Central Body is the most massive of the bodies in an orbital system.</dc:description>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">central body</rdfs:label>
    <ns1:Alternative_Label xml:lang="en">Central Body</ns1:Alternative_Label>
    <ns1:Alternative_Label xml:lang="en">Central Mass</ns1:Alternative_Label>
    <ns1:Alternative_Label xml:lang="en">Primary</ns1:Alternative_Label>
    <ns1:Alternative_Label xml:lang="en">Primary Body</ns1:Alternative_Label>
    <ns1:Alternative_Label xml:lang="en">Primary Mass</ns1:Alternative_Label>
    <ns1:Development_Status_Note xml:lang="en">The central body (or central mass, or primary body) of a multi-body gravitational system (an orbital system, e.g., solar system) is the more massive of the bodies in the system. In other words, it is the body around which all other bodies in the system orbit. The concept of a central body (or central mass) thereby may reflect a context-specific situation. It may be a relative concept, and always in relation to one or more other entities, and with respect to an observer. A central body is considered relative to a given orbital system, i.e. a specific set of bodies. The central body of our solar system is the Sun, but is the Earth of the Earth-moon system. It can therefore be ontologically modeled in a couple of ways. One is as a role played by a celestial body. A body that is assigned the role of central body by an observer.</ns1:Development_Status_Note>
  </rdf:Description>
