    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purl.org/space-ontology/Space_Mission_Segment"/>
    <dc:creator rdf:resource="http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3835-7817"/>
    <dc:creator xml:lang="en">Robert John Rovetto</dc:creator>
    <dc:description xml:lang="en">A space mission, and the SSA domain, is often desribed as having segments: the ground segment, control segment, launch segment, space segment, user segment, etc. Each represents a grouping of sysetms, activities, and personnel that form part of and realize the overall mission, or SSA system.</dc:description>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">space segment</rdfs:label>
    <ns1:Clarifying_Note xml:lang="en">A spacecraft mission, and the outerspace domain in general, is often described in terms of segments: the ground segment, control segment, launch segment, space segment, user segment, etc. Each represents a grouping of sysetms, activities, and personnel that form part of, and help execute the mission or operate the SSA system.</ns1:Clarifying_Note>
    <ns1:Development_Status_Note xml:lang="en">This is a tentative category to group the space-based systems that are part (a segment of) an astronautical mission or SSA system</ns1:Development_Status_Note>
  </rdf:Description>
