  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://purl.org/space-ontology/Preferred_Label">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty"/>
    <dc:creator rdf:resource="http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3835-7817"/>
    <dc:description xml:lang="en">The preferred label (term) of the given entity/concept.

Where a given entity/concept in the ontology has alternative labels (labels or terms that communicate/express the same intended meaninig, e.g., equivalent or synonymous terms) a preferred one will be selected.</dc:description>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The Preferred Label annotation indicates the preferred natural language label (term or word phrase) for a particular ontology construct (class, property, individual, etc.). It will most likely be the label indicated by the rdfs:label annotation. It may be composed of one or more words. It can be understood as the name of the given intended meaning or definition.

The preferred label, and rdfs:label, should have a form that most closely expresses, matches, and is most easily understood as expressing, the intended meaning of associated (or corresponding) ontology construct. For example, a label composed of multiple words should have words whose meaning is easily understood and whose arrangement most closely expresses the intended meaning of the whole construct.

In other words, the preferred label, and rdfs:label, should capture the natural language definition as closely as possible.

The intended meaning of a created class, relation or indvidiual should corresponds closely with its preferred label. 

The preferred label should have a form that most closely corresponds to, and is most easily understood as expressing, the intended meaning.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Preferred Label</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
