  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://purl.org/space-ontology/Observation_Dataset">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purl.org/space-ontology/SSA_Data"/>
    <dc:creator rdf:resource="http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3835-7817"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The dataset or measurement, of a given object in orbit, produced by a sensor that detects or observs that object.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The term 'observation' in the space domain community is often used ambiguously to refer to the activity of observing, or the actual dataset that is the result or output of that activity. That is, it's often used to signify the resultant particular observation data of a specific sensor.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Observation Dataset</rdfs:label>
    <ns1:Development_Status_Note xml:lang="en">Under development. 
'observation dataset' vs. 'observation'</ns1:Development_Status_Note>
  </rdf:Description>
