  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://purl.org/space-ontology/Orbital_Property">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purl.org/space-ontology/Physical_Property"/>
    <dc:creator rdf:resource="http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3835-7817"/>
    <dc:creator xml:lang="en">Robert John Rovetto</dc:creator>
    <dc:description xml:lang="en">A property, feature, parameter, quality, or characteristic of an orbit.</dc:description>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Orbital Property</rdfs:label>
    <ns1:Description_of_Class xml:lang="en">This class is intended to categorize various feature of orbits, e.g., the classical orbital elements, apoapsis, perigee, etc.</ns1:Description_of_Class>
    <ns1:Development_Status_Note xml:lang="en">Ongoing development.

The orbital features, such as apogee, can have corresponding numeric measurement values (captured by OWL Data Properties such as has_orbital_property_value, has_Apogee_measurement_value, has_quantitative_measurement, etc.). 

In this way, an Orbit or a Spacecraft class or instance can be related to the Orbital Property and the specific (instance) value of the property at a given time.
Example: Orbit has_Apogee Apogee and Apogee has_Apogee_value 2000 km.

Alternatively, if no property classes are desired, then OWL Data Properties may suffice. The value would take a particular data type (integer, etc.). Example: Orbit has_Apogee_meaurement_value 2000 km.

Likewise can be done for the dates and times of events, e.g. mission execution event, orbital maneuver event, launch date, orbital conjunction time, etc.</ns1:Development_Status_Note>
    <ns1:Example xml:lang="en">Orbital eccentricity, inclination, semimajor axis, etc.</ns1:Example>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://purl.org/space-ontology/Propagation_Process">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purl.org/space-ontology/SSA_Process"/>
    <dc:creator rdf:resource="http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3835-7817"/>
    <dc:description xml:lang="en">The propagation process in an SSA context involves the prediction of spacecraft future positions by considering past and current obervations (observational data).</dc:description>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Propagation Process</rdfs:label>
    <ns1:Alternative_Label xml:lang="en">Prediction Process</ns1:Alternative_Label>
  </rdf:Description>
