Considering alternative definitions.
Consider time-relative relations, such as has_Orbit_at-time or has_Orbit_at-Epoch.</ns1:Development_Status_Note>
    <ns1:Intended_Meaning_of_Ontology_Construct xml:lang="en">This OWL Object Property is intended to represent the relation between a natural or artificial mass and its orbit.</ns1:Intended_Meaning_of_Ontology_Construct>
  </rdf:Description>
