  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://purl.org/space-ontology/Satellite_Catalog_Number">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purl.org/space-ontology/Identifier"/>
    <dc:creator rdf:resource="http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3835-7817"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">satellite catalog number</rdfs:label>
    <ns1:Development_Status_Note xml:lang="en">Distinguish between the catalog number used in particular catalogs such as the US DoD SATCAT, and the generic category of Spacecraft Catalog Number.

Consider different modeling approaches. One, use a generic 'Identifier' class together with a relation such as 'is-assigned-by' to link the particular spacecraft number to the database, organization or agent that assigns and owns the number. 
Example: 
Spacecraft-001 has-Identifier A001
A001 is-instance-of Identifier
A001 is-assigned-by COSPAR.

Two, a hierachy of spacecraft identifier clases, each of which are for specific organizations or databases.
Example:
Spacecraft-001 has-COSPAR-ID A001
A001 is-instance-of COSPAR_ID
COSPAR_ID is-a-subclass-of Identifier.</ns1:Development_Status_Note>
  </rdf:Description>
