  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://purl.org/space-ontology/Natural_Language_Definition_of_Label">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty"/>
    <dc:creator rdf:resource="http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3835-7817"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statement, in natural language, expressing the intended meaning of the label (term or word) assigned to the selected ontology element/concept/construct (class, relation, indivdiual, etc.). It is a definition of the preferred or rendered/displayed label.

In other words, the annotation provides the definition of the label assigned to the selected ontology class, relation, or indivdiual.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Natural Language Definition of Label</rdfs:label>
    <ns1:Development_Status_Note xml:lang="en">Further development needed.

This annotation provides, in natural language, the intended meaning of the preferred label (term) of the selected ontology construct (i.e., class, relation, indvidiual,, etc.). It is a definition of at least the preferred label term, if not alternative or synonymous label terms.

This reflects a distinction between the description of the construct, and the definition of the label it is given. rdfs:ccomment and dc:description may be seen as similar, but the idea is to make the distinction explicit, i.e., to show the finer detail. Consider this: a desription of the term 'dog' may be 'a three-lettered word that...', whereas the definition of 'dog' may be 'a three-legged mammal that...'. 

Therefore, the preferred/rendered label (i.e., term) for the construct should have a meaning (definition) that matches it. The two should match--they should express similar, if not the same, intended meaning.

If, however, a label definition is not the same as this, then a definition annotation should provide a more structured definition.

Examples of ontology elements or constructs are Classes, Object Properites and Annotation Properties in Protege.</ns1:Development_Status_Note>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://purl.org/space-ontology/Definition"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://purl.org/space-ontology/Cite_as">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty"/>
    <dc:creator rdf:resource="http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3835-7817"/>
    <dc:description xml:lang="en">This note desribes what information should be included when citing or referencing the ontology (in a publication or other work), e.g., the name of the creator (author), associated publicaiton(s), current title of the ontology, website, etc. It provides an example citation. Any standard citation format may be used.</dc:description>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Cite as</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
